* ci(detect): fall back to the merge commit's git diff when the compare API fails [daveey]

Every PR macOS state job queued 01:20-05:00Z on 2026-11-11 came from a
detect that failed open: the compare call hit 'API rate limit exceeded for
installation' (HTTP 403) three times, the classifier got no files and turned
every lane on, so 16 PRs that touch no state code queued the one-runner
macOS state lane (~9 h at 34 min/job). Example: PR #1066 touches only
tui_gateway/agent files; classify() on its list gives hermes_state=false.

The action now uses git diff of the checked-out PR merge commit against its
first parent when the API fails. git fetch does not spend the REST quota. It is
used only when HEAD equals GITHUB_SHA and the merge's second parent equals the
event head SHA; otherwise, or with an empty diff, it fails open as before.
--no-renames lists a rename under both names.

Proof: tests/ci/test_detect_changes_git_fallback.py runs the action's own
bash against a real depth-1 merge checkout with a rate-limited gh: unrelated
change skips the state lane, state change and state rename select it,
unverified checkouts fail open. Four mutants (each guard, rename mode, the
fallback call) are each killed. tests/ci classify/macos routing/update routing
pass (323).

