* fix(kanban): a far quota wall moves a non-mandatory model pin to a same-class peer, one run at a time [daveey]

example-tools M4 (t_01a19715a1a9ccef) was pinned to gpt-6-astra/openai-codex. Run 49 ended
rate_limited with the Codex reset ~56 h out, and the quota episode held the card for the whole
wall: an explicit pin had no alternate route, workers cannot re-pin a card (set-model is fenced),
and no supervisor model-edit op exists. Three runners-board cards (K2 t_01a188c7c974c529,
shepherd t_82f80db4, H3 t_174a18ae) stranded on the same pin. David approved option (b),
11-11 (t_01a19990897b9d9b): pins are reroutable within their class unless marked mandatory.

Rule (hermes_cli/kanban_pin_reroute.py `pinned_route`). Every condition must hold; anything
else keeps the pin and today's hold:
1. one of the card's own runs hit a wall on the pin's provider (quota_episode receipts or the
   live episode), and the wall is still up;
2. it resets kanban.pin_quota_reroute_min_hours (default 6) or more from now;
3. the pin is not mandatory (new tasks.model_pin_mandatory, or the require_model marker);
4. the lane is ready, not review;
5. the pinned model is in exactly one routing class of the assignee's policy, and a route of
   that class is eligible, off every walled/disabled provider and not live-walled. No fallback to
   default_model or the strong tier.

Rule 1 reads the card's history, not only the live episode: a rerouted run that ends
(reclaimed, continued) closes the episode, and the next run must not go back into the wall.

Invariants:
- the pin row is never written; the reroute is on the in-memory claimed task, so the first run
  after the reset uses the pin again (run_route reason `pinned`);
- every rerouted admission records a `model_reroute` event (from/to, walled provider,
  resets_at, episode_id, run_id) and tier reason `pinned+pin_quota_reroute:<provider>`, with
  one card comment per wall naming the opt-out command;
- if that record cannot be written the run keeps its pin (reason
  `pinned+pin_quota_reroute_unrecorded`): no unrecorded reroute;
- a mandatory pin is never moved.

Mandatory mark: nullable tasks.model_pin_mandatory (migration via _LATER_TASK_COLUMNS, Board
sync column), set by kanban_create(pin_mandatory=true), `hermes kanban create --pin-mandatory`
and `hermes kanban set-model <id> [--mandatory|--no-mandatory]`; clearing the pin clears it,
a new pin keeps it. Workers stay fenced. kanban_assignment_routing's no-model-edit message
now says the dispatcher handles quota walls.

