* fix(kanban): continuation review fixes: update-gap wait, one prepare per session [daveey]

- Worker: a refusal gap past OWNER_WAIT_S checks the board for this attempt's unconsumed checkpoint; the
  hermes update path (restart wait refuses, then the tree moves) never shows a terminal receipt first,
  so without this the worker gave up at OWNER_WAIT_S and the run was reclaimed anyway.
- Owner: prepare() is serialized per session, so a retried kanban.run racing the first cannot append a
  second synthetic result for the same interrupted tool call.
- Drop the _require_admission_open pre-check before prepare (the admission submit already refuses on a
  draining owner; the pre-check only refused earlier with a different error).
- test_core_update_kanban_wait pins the checkpoint the managed Stop booking passes.

Proof: new tests killed by mutants R1 (no board check -> update-gap test fails), R2 (no per-session lock
-> race test writes two tool results), R3 (checkpoint kwargs dropped -> booking test fails).

* fix(kanban): a restart-cut tool call carries the update-pause result in the real stop path [daveey]

Review of c1570eb7001: a clean restart Stop hard-interrupts the managed child, whose own executor then
answers the cut-off call (a killed command's '[Command interrupted]' output, or the abandoned/skipped
cancel text) and closes the turn with assistant rows. The continuation only answered calls left with
no result, so the spec's '[interrupted by Hermes update at <UTC>: re-run if still needed]' was never
written; the model saw replay cleanup's orphan-recovery notice instead.

- prepare() now rewrites, in place (a result must stay right after its call), the stopped turn's
  cancelled/skipped/interrupted tool results: the tool rows after the last assistant tool-call
  message, past the closing assistant rows and nothing else. A finished call's result, or any tool row
  before a later user turn, is never touched. Idempotent: the rewritten text matches none of them.
- Worker: claim.continuing is cleared once a turn is admitted, so after the continuation a final owner
  answer is final again (not an uncounted restart loss) and owner silence gets OWNER_WAIT_S.
- Correction to c1570eb7001's message: dropping the _require_admission_open pre-check means a draining
  owner can record the continuation marker before submit refuses runtime_draining; the next owner then
  reuses that same marker/request id (same as admit_claim for a first admission).

Proof: the real two-owner probe gains a mid_tool_call case (SIGTERM while the turn's terminal call
runs 'sleep 120'): the continued turn's model request carries exactly the update-pause text for that
call (before this commit: the orphan-recovery notice). Mutants S1-S7 on the new conditions all killed.

* fix(kanban): a turn stopped before its child bootstrapped is not continued [daveey]

Review of 23ce3427a4a: admit_managed checkpointed every restart-caused interruption, including a stop
during child spawn/startup (_interrupted_before_bootstrap) when the turn never ran. For an attempt
started from a copied transcript the session is non-empty, so the next owner continued it with only
the continuation note (skipping this run's first prompt, skills and resume note) and could rewrite the
previous run's trailing cancelled tool results. Such a stop is now booked without a checkpoint: the
plain uncounted requeue (with transcript copy), as before this change.

Proof: test_a_stop_before_the_child_bootstrapped_is_not_a_checkpoint; mutant B1 (flag ignored) killed.

